Build-time tools (not linked into programs, not shipped)
========================================================

quench_shaderc runs on the build machine only and links these; their licence texts are in their source archives
(cmake/ShaderToolchain.cmake pins them):

- glslang: BSD-3-Clause, BSD-2-Clause, MIT and Apache-2.0 for different parts (its LICENSE.txt)
- SPIRV-Tools: Apache-2.0
- SPIRV-Cross: Apache-2.0
- SPIRV-Headers: MIT
- DXC: University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source License (its LICENSE.TXT; ThirdPartyNotices.txt lists the parts
  under other permissive licences). On Windows hosts the release archive (cmake/ShaderToolchain.cmake); on other
  hosts v1.9.2609 (commit 01b62ad47db7dee3dd33f90e7339cf9e860b3f93) built from source with its submodules
  SPIRV-Headers (MIT), SPIRV-Tools (Apache-2.0) and DirectX-Headers (MIT) at the commits that tag records
  (cmake/BuildDxc.cmake); it compiles only the shader entries that use ray queries. Both licence files are kept
  next to the built dxc in the tool cache.

quench_cook, the asset cooker (cmake/CookToolchain.cmake pins fastgltf, stb and astc-encoder; fastgltf pins and
hash-checks the simdjson and simdutf files it downloads), links:

- fastgltf v1.0.0 (commit 0b800b4a584704f9e9add67c79c4c8732e552787): MIT
- astc-encoder 5.7.1 (commit 0affb51aaf0e0de3a8b038fa32487d59754a1eed), its library sources only: Apache-2.0
  (its LICENSE.txt; no NOTICE file). It writes the ASTC 4x4 textures; the programs read them without it.
- simdjson 5.1.0 and simdutf 9.3.3 (bundled by fastgltf): Apache-2.0 or MIT, at the user's choice
- stb_image (stb commit 003501f6d7a8668ce8b6d875e34dd97ad0d5d5b5): MIT or public domain
- Basis Universal v2.50 (above; cmake/QuenchBasisu.cmake), its encoder library: Apache-2.0 with the NOTICE above;
  bundled in it jpgd (public domain or Apache-2.0), pvpngreader (public domain), android_astc_decomp (Apache-2.0, the
  Android Open Source Project), tinyexr (BSD-3-Clause), qoi and tinydds (MIT), and the full Zstandard (zstd/zstd.c,
  BSD-3-Clause) for UASTC's supercompression. It writes the Basis Universal textures; the programs read them with the
  transcoder.
- bc7enc.cpp of bc7enc_rdo (above): MIT or public domain
- meshoptimizer (above): MIT
- miniaudio (above, through quench_audio): public domain or MIT No Attribution
- ozz-animation (above): MIT
